"settings.autoCorrectEnter" = "Fix on Enter (new line only)";
"settings.autoCorrectSimilar" = "Between similar layouts (experimental)";
"settings.autoCorrectSimilar.tip" = "Converts a word typed on a layout of one language that reads as another language of the same script, e.g. German typed on the English layout (“yeit” → “zeit”), and the other way round. The two languages are told apart only by their distinctive letters, so words common to both are left alone and some wrong ones slip through. Pairs such as en ↔ de or uk ↔ ru. Available only when two layouts of one script and different languages are enabled, e.g. English and German.";
"settings.autoCorrectSpell" = "Check with the system dictionary (experimental)";
"settings.autoCorrectSpell.tip" = "Asks the system spelling dictionary before converting: a real word is left alone even when it looks odd, and a word the dictionary knows only in the other layout is converted. Also fixes one typo in a word typed in the wrong layout (“рудддщ” → “hello”) when the dictionary leaves a single candidate. Available only when the system has a spelling dictionary for the language of an enabled layout.";
"settings.autoCorrectUnavailable" = "Auto-correct needs keyboard layouts of different scripts, e.g. English and any Cyrillic one. Layouts of one script (%@) can't be told apart reliably — use the hotkey.";

